// A UFCS method call on a module-global struct, where the method takes
// `self: *T`, mutates the GLOBAL's live storage — not a stack copy. Each
// `g.bump()` increments the same `g`, so after three calls `g.n == 3`.
//
// Alloca+storing the receiver of a `*Self` method on
// a global into a throwaway copy loses mutations through `self` (the global
// stays 0). Locals and explicit `@g` are unaffected; only the
// UFCS-on-global path copies. fixupMethodReceiver addresses the
// global's `global_addr` directly.

Counter :: struct {
    n: i64 = 0;
    bump :: (self: *Counter) { self.n += 1; }
}

g : Counter = .{};

main :: () -> i32 {
    g.bump();
    g.bump();
    g.bump();
    return xx g.n;   // 3
}
